From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopfire <hgrmeanwhile@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:02:41 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(provider): add the Command Code provider to the v2
 orchestrator

Ports the Command Code provider from main's implementation (upstream
PR #10861) to the v2 orchestration stack. Main's drivers expose
`adapter` (ProviderAdapterShape) while this stack's drivers expose
`orchestrationAdapter` (ProviderAdapterV2Shape), so the provider is
re-ported at the orchestration boundary rather than merged.

What changed at the boundary:

- The NDJSON protocol layer is reused unchanged: parseCommandCodeNdjsonLine
  (now in CommandCodeAdapterV2.ts), commandCodeTurnArgs, and
  parseCommandCodeModelList are byte-identical to main's modules.
- The v1 session/sendTurn shape became openSession -> session runtime:
  ensureThread/resumeThread register a thread and adopt the persisted
  Command Code session id from the provider thread's nativeThreadRef;
  startTurn spawns the per-turn `-p` subprocess inside the session scope
  and returns immediately, streaming turn items/messages/nodes through
  the runtime's event queue and closing with turn.terminal.
- Interrupt/Stop is a clean abort: a signal-killed child's failed exit
  wait folds into the exit-code decision and terminalizes as
  "interrupted", never a provider failure (matches main's packaging
  patch behavior).
- Mid-turn steering: the v2 orchestrator routes mid-turn sends to
  steerTurn by itself (CommandPolicy active_steering), so the "a turn is
  already running" rejection from main does not exist here; the adapter
  queues the steered prompt on the active run and drains it as the same
  provider turn once the current CLI process exits, resuming the same
  Command Code session. A turn that fails or is interrupted names its
  undelivered steers in a system_notice instead of dropping them
  silently.
- Capabilities advertise what headless mode can do: no approvals, no
  rollback/fork/snapshot, no session model switch (models apply per
  turn via --model), active steering on.
- Wiring: CommandCodeDriver composes the v2 adapter, the status-probe
  snapshot (version + --list-models catalog, auth unknown), and the
  unsupported-text-generation seam; registered in BUILT_IN_DRIVERS and
  the v2 adapter driver inventory. Contracts add the commandCode driver
  settings (binary path, permission mode, launch args), the legacy
  providers record + patch entries, and the display name. Web settings
  get a data-driven client definition.

Verified with the mock-CLI fixtures ported to v2 (turn streaming,
session resume, interrupt, mid-turn steer, failed-steer accounting),
the NDJSON parser fixture tests, and the --list-models parser tests.

Work done by ZCode (cmd/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash).
